and opposition supporters rallied in Delhi and Mumbai on Sunday to demand the resignation of India's election commission chief over changes to ​voter rolls as ‌police detained some demonstrators for a third day.</summary></entry><entry><title>North Korea launches ballistic missile as tensions with Seoul grow over border mine blasts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb9c98ed8aa6201e0182160a04cc3c1f7ba5026e0dbd698b6af9fbf9757cb505</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T02:40:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261003-north-korea-fires-ballistic-missile-after-seoul-s-apology-demand--31f42c33e2e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261003-north-korea-fires-ballistic-missile-after-seoul-s-apology-demand" /><summary type="html">North Korea launched a ballistic missile Saturday morning from the Wonsan area on its east coast into the Sea of Japan, according to South Korea's military. The launch comes amid renewed tensions between Pyongyang and Seoul, with the latter demanding an apology for a blast that wounded three South Korean soldiers inside the Demilitarized Zone last month.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'Make our streets safer!' Mass women's protests sweep India over sexual violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd2a31df850e09ae913a1d701dec2172a5d57f0a6facf63b5e811441da535d42</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:57:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261002-make-our-streets-safer-mass-women-s-protests-sweep-india-over-sexual-violence--825117eadd3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261002-make-our-streets-safer-mass-women-s-protests-sweep-india-over-sexual-violence" /><summary type="html">In India, thousands of women have been taking to the streets calling for better protection of female students, following the suspected gang rape of a 17-year-old girl. The alleged incident in an upscale neighbourhood of New Delhi prompted authorities to beef up protective measures, but the women say limiting their access to public spaces is not the answer.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Thailand floods: At least 8 die, thousands move to shelters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6044bbc85687f4e3a2fd2a6fa7eee9356283d53b447d0a945af373a6239137f</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T11:20:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-thailand-floods-at-least-8-die-thousands-move-to-shelters--915a2d7132c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260928-thailand-floods-at-least-8-die-thousands-move-to-shelters" /><summary type="html">Rain eased in Thailand ’s capital on Sunday, but flooding persisted in several low-lying areas, with thousands forced to move into temporary shelters. At least eight people were reported killed in the past 10 days nationwide.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands evacuated amid Bangkok floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:037e5e0b7b9f06e8897f3ff2c06705a903c4f7cd0304986dd5d04ff8892311f5</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-evacuated-amid-bangkok-floods--f805440afd9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-evacuated-amid-bangkok-floods" /><summary type="html">Rain is easing in Thailand’s capital, but flooding continues in several low-lying areas. Thousands of people have been forced into temporary shelters after the government declared Bangkok a disaster zone on Saturday. At least eight people have died over the past 10 days as heavy rains caused widespread disruption. Juliette Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>A month after, thousands are still missing and families face a long recovery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c00b089ef34fd5240a99dd4de5f7673484415ad7cf1c1983f807081a008984df</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:40:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-month-after-thousands-are-still-missing-and-families-face-a-long-recovery--547bee35856b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-month-after-thousands-are-still-missing-and-families-face-a-long-recovery" /><summary type="html">A month after Nepal’s floods, thousands are still missing and families face a long recovery.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bangkok declares flood disaster after massive 48-hour downpour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c7847d4fe5e57572d8173bf7d3e1968f478e8d1847985b148f5985e24615807</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T04:40:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260926-bangkok-declares-flood-disaster-after-massive-48h-downpour--629faecd1f1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260926-bangkok-declares-flood-disaster-after-massive-48h-downpour" /><summary type="html">Thailand’s capital Bangkok declared a flood disaster on Saturday after more than 300 millimetres of rain in less than 48 hours, leaving canals overflowing and streets submerged. “It’s like at my waist level now,” a local said. The governor has urged people not to panic, saying the situation is stabilising.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Fatalities on Indian roads: One death reported every three minutes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d415340827440057e2dd716579d142a1bb5a4a1b407d3125ef1b8d2f57a4476</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:33:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260925-fatalities-on-indian-roads-one-death-reported-every-three-minutes--b0b4970ad80e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260925-fatalities-on-indian-roads-one-death-reported-every-three-minutes" /><summary type="html">India has the second-largest road network in the world, spanning over 6 million kilometres. But these roads are silent killers, with one death reported every three minutes. Every day, headlines are filled with horror stories: drunk drivers mowing people down, school buses hit by speeding trucks killing children, buses with dozens of passengers plunging into gorges.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Journalism and resistance under Taliban rule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:625c80b4e9c3dcf6618fa058ff8f8c1ddc4e54183af7765fa52344c939e11d26</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T10:21:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260925-journalism-and-resistance-under-taliban-rule--1976c788e5fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260925-journalism-and-resistance-under-taliban-rule" /><summary type="html">In this edition, we focus on Afghanistan, which recently marked the fifth anniversary of the Taliban's return to power. Since then, the exclusion of women and girls has become normalised, with the government systematically dismantling the rights of more than half the country's population.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal’s catastrophic floods were ‘warning to the world', PM Shah tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:580676e335c6df50e4769d973b90dabb5c319799485000543979e482e8931ca0</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T01:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260925-nepal-floods-warning-world-pm-shah-un--2fd13a540ae2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260925-nepal-floods-warning-world-pm-shah-un" /><summary type="html">Nepal’s Prime Minister Balendra Shah said on Thursday that last month’s catastrophic floods were a “warning to the world” of growing climate risks in the Himalayas. He said warming was melting glaciers and permafrost and urged international support to help Nepal adapt to threats it could not face alone.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'Trump views US-China relations as a personal friendship: Xi views US as an adversary to be managed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d97f0b7711a099704e3293feed9e6900d4738905df78148eb809f2b49c37591a</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed--29eaaa0e21d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Henrietta Levin, Senior Fellow with the Freeman Chair in China Studies at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. The US remains a powerful actor in its relationship with China. But power on paper is not the same thing as leverage at the negotiating table. Levin warns that President Trump’s highly personalized approach to Xi Jinping offers Beijing opportunities that China can easily exploit. Xi does not approach the relationship in the same way. Au contraire, he sees the United States as an adversary to be managed while China pursues its domestic priorities and strategic objectives in Asia, including on Taiwan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Taiwan: Home of semiconductor giants at the centre of AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2448617ba74257fe43746c2e93cfcec96a0333b71aac92d91d1fa27359d87c87</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race--f4a0e175142c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race" /><summary type="html">The topic of artificial intelligence looms large as Chinese President Xi Jinping begins his highly anticipated state visit to Washington. The fate of Taiwan – coveted by its larger neighbour, China – will also be on the table. It's the global leader in superconductor research and development. These powerful chips can be found in smartphones, computers, and above all in AI development. Our France 2 colleagues take a rare look inside one of Taiwan's state-of-the-art laboratories.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan launches air strikes in Afghanistan, killing civilians, Taliban says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:400097dbd0e7279ec6eecc3c1da194c218f144627b0ecd3ca82b27fa06e39b82</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T08:53:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260924-pakistan-launches-air-strikes-in-afghanistan-killing-civilians-taliban-says--7caa8e352d5c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260924-pakistan-launches-air-strikes-in-afghanistan-killing-civilians-taliban-says" /><summary type="html">Pakistan launched air strikes Thursday on 10 sites in Afghanistan in what Islamabad said was a retaliation for a drone attack by Afghanistan's Taliban forces on a border post. A Taliban government spokesman denied the allegation and said Pakistan's latest strikes killed four civilians in Afghanistan's southern and eastern provinces.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>China cracks down on scam centres in neighbouring Myanmar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4348e6ac83d3229fa0c486abb3455599bec7ebaa0e3a1132978273c6aaaf4305</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:01:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260923-china-cracks-down-on-scam-centres-in-neighbouring-myanmar--6eaea5ec0493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260923-china-cracks-down-on-scam-centres-in-neighbouring-myanmar" /><summary type="html">In Southeast Asia, hundreds of thousands of people working in fraud centres are scamming people across the world. US authorities suggest the fraudsters are responsible for scams worth almost $10 billion a year against US nationals alone. Victims in Europe, the UK and China have also been targeted. Human rights groups further warn that those working in the centres are often themselves victims of human trafficking – forced to work as slaves.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Sri Lanka: 15 convicted over Easter bombings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b90596e1b728ba7257c19d1681b6d8540a73c1788c6cbdb4b335a399821a9692</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:36:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sri-lanka-15-convicted-over-easter-bombings--22aa604a66ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sri-lanka-15-convicted-over-easter-bombings" /><summary type="html">Sri Lanka’s 2019 Easter bombings, one of the deadliest attacks in the country’s history, killed more than 260 people. After a trial lasting nearly five years, 15 men have now been convicted over the attacks, which were inspired by the Islamic State group. All those convicted are members of Sri Lanka’s Muslim minority. Ellen Gainsford reports on their sentences.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pakistan arrests sisters of imprisoned former PM Imran Khan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18906bab614402ac27fa7eebf5b4bf8e315b670766b6acd922643e13fedb3231</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T07:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260921-sisters-of-jailed-former-pakistani-pm-imran-khan-arrested--ad35916c88df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260921-sisters-of-jailed-former-pakistani-pm-imran-khan-arrested" /><summary type="html">The three sisters of former Pakistani prime minister Imran Khan were arrested in the province of Punjab, his Tehreek-e-Insaf party said on Monday. Khan, who was prime minister from 2018 to 2022, has been imprisoned since 2023 and was sentenced last year to 17 years on corruption charges.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires two ballistic missiles into the sea in latest weapons display</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15f501db39e166528fb933dce9294429855d8245ec41faae2ff0d93872c4991f</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T11:40:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260920-north-korea-fires-two-ballistic-missiles-into-the-sea-in-latest-weapons-display--e0338db75d93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260920-north-korea-fires-two-ballistic-missiles-into-the-sea-in-latest-weapons-display" /><summary type="html">North Korea fired two short-range ballistic missiles into the sea off its eastern coast on Sunday, South Korea’s military said. This came days after Pyongyang reaffirmed its status as a nuclear-armed state and rejected a UN resolution calling for an end to its nuclear activities.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Japan under pressure amid accommodation woes as Asian Games kick off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c939d9e5851038c68a3dca83e5ba04aac81da125f2c801e929abe362126f3de0</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T10:02:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/japan-under-pressure-amid-accommodation-woes-as-asian-games-kick-off--c800f315db92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/japan-under-pressure-amid-accommodation-woes-as-asian-games-kick-off" /><summary type="html">It’s the world's biggest sporting event, held every four years – the 20th edition of Asian games is starting in Japan. Organisers came under pressure even before competition began… as thousands more athletes and officials registered to take part than initially expected. Story by Charlotte Lam.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI safety: No, China will not hit the brakes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6de60110ab3b8d5fe5314b988523f66d66bdb4dc042f2a2841eca9059c0e14d2</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:40:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260918-ai-safety-no-china-will-not-hit-the-brakes--a3a1637a9405.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260918-ai-safety-no-china-will-not-hit-the-brakes" /><summary type="html">A spate of warnings in recent days about the dangers of AI have sparked mixed reactions: from Donald Trump dismissing the fears as a hoax, to Beijing criticising calls for the US to block its advancement as fearmongering. As President Xi Jinping heads to Washington for talks, FRANCE 24's technology correspondent Peter O'Brien explains why the two superpowers are unlikely to forge binding agreements on AI regulation.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>India vows to protect energy security after new US tariffs over Russian oil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fab0b8204784c763bbed7716e9ecfadaf406c11b8386f13e4e8bb566368e2c6c</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T18:50:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/india-vows-to-protect-energy-security-after-new-us-tariffs-over-russian-oil--8b7b9fba5796.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/india-vows-to-protect-energy-security-after-new-us-tariffs-over-russian-oil" /><summary type="html">India has warned Washington that new measures to levy tariffs over the purchase of Russian oil could impact bilateral ties, the South Asian nation's foreign ministry said on Thursday, hours after the U.S. made a ​new move to ‌punish such buyers. Earlier in the day, the U.S. House of Representatives passed a sweeping sanctions and tariff bill intended ⁠to increase economic pressure on Russia over its invasion of Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Erdogan to sidestep Turkey’s constitutional term limits in early 2028 vote, adviser says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76a62fb225687004d538676fd64fd0bf4ffe11e7ec7f1a44cde19a67953dc971</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260917-turkey-s-erdogan-to-run-in-early-2028-vote-sidestepping-constitutional-term-limit--a36ab3db2bec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260917-turkey-s-erdogan-to-run-in-early-2028-vote-sidestepping-constitutional-term-limit" /><summary type="html">Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan intends to run in an early election in 2028 in order to circumvent the constitutional term limits he would face if he serves out his full current term, a top adviser said Thursday. Under Turkey's constitution, parliament can trigger early elections given the support of 360 lawmakers, meaning the ruling AKP and its nationalist ally MHP will need support of at least 34 more lawmakers.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong unveils first five-year plan to cement position as global financial hub</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab443849a71fcdefa27b8e76084931b89a174195f12a4f0d124af25c95d69f86</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T05:54:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260916-hong-kong-unveils-first-five-year-plan-to-cement-position-as-global-financial-hub--56f27ec8290b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260916-hong-kong-unveils-first-five-year-plan-to-cement-position-as-global-financial-hub" /><summary type="html">Hong ⁠Kong leader ​John Lee on Wednesday unveiled the city's first five-year plan to boost its global position as a financial hub. The plan serves as a social and economic roadmap detailing the city-state's strategic priorities, including an aim to expand technology ties with mainland China.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>China projecting image of 'stabilising force in world politics', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ff8cc4c5f19514814e92b3367fb6427aad74b4cc3abdd24d2dd59e86e1fc2f5</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T21:06:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260915-china-projecting-image-of-stabilising-force-in-world-politics-expert-says--48ed2a17448e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260915-china-projecting-image-of-stabilising-force-in-world-politics-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Rex Li, Professor of International Relations at King's College London, says that China "is trying to promote an alternative international security order and project itself as a stabilising force in world politics", adding that while Beijing "is increasingly willing to play a more significant part in ending the conflict in the Middle East, so far we haven't seen any concrete proposals coming from China".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>China projecting image of 'stabilising force in world politics', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2a7e2729af1820ee96f80fef7fdd52e9a12e09f134e2e1f652f23ffa0d9821a</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T21:04:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/china-projecting-image-of-stabilising-force-in-world-politics-expert-says--5cc52bcb6cf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/china-projecting-image-of-stabilising-force-in-world-politics-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Rex Li, Professor of International Relations at King's College London, says that China "is trying to promote an alternative international security order and project itself as a stabilising force in world politics", adding that while Beijing "is increasingly willing to play a more significant part in ending the conflict in the Middle East, so far we haven't seen any concrete proposals coming from China".</summary></entry><entry><title>Viral Putin, Modi and Xi selfie at BRICS summit is AI-generated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef0862749703e4333fb2e479c01e1842727298fd4718ea3be58fafc3144ae870</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:49:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260915-viral-putin-modi-and-xi-selfie-at-brics-summit-is-ai-generated--c818ffc4f677.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260915-viral-putin-modi-and-xi-selfie-at-brics-summit-is-ai-generated" /><summary type="html">A viral selfie allegedly showing leaders including, Russian President Vladimir Putin, Chinese President Xi Jinping and Indian Prime Minister Narendra at the BRICS summit in New Delhi is AI-generated. A SynthID watermark shows it was created using OpenAI tools. Several leaders pictured, including Brazil’s Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and Turkey’s Recep Tayyip Erdoğan, did not attend. Another AI selfie features former Iranian president Ebrahim Raisi, who died in 2024. Both images were widely shared online, including by official embassy accounts. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey police disperse pro-LGBTQ protesters with tear gas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9ea220d22d1cd76d98f1c7dd29c9866ff881f0c7fb63b458c55aa3a7a91c65c</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:54:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas--85ad9b6b4b9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas" /><summary type="html">Turkish police fired tear gas at pro-LGBTQ demonstrators in the western city of Izmir on Monday, as activists protested a nationwide crackdown that saw dozens arrested over the weekend in a campaign authorities described as defending traditional family values.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'What makes China work despite the pain in society?' asks analyst Dan Wang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5d33f89de6b1133707b67c5afd8b7277a413ac074c350709c0ffa1490b1f679</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:30:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang--d40c2ced80a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, FRANCE 24’s Stuart Norval speaks to Dan Wang, a China expert whose book ‘Breakneck:  China’s Quest to Engineer the Future’ is a New York Times bestseller. It takes a close look at Chinese life and draws from Wang’s own ten years of living there. Wang says the China and the US are some of the most similar people in the world, as they are both hustlers and take shortcuts.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Climate catastrophe leaves Nepal mourning while the search for the missing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37e27908b2c9bf83f79b74bbee12b65eb87cd1026b97dfd5de9d83b117d3d0de</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues--40d634ca2dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues" /><summary type="html">The himalayan flash flood that devastated northern Nepal on August 26 was an unprecedented disaster. The death toll continues to rise, with nearly 1,400 people now confirmed dead and 5,130 still missing, including around 600 foreign nationals from 35 countries.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia: Rescuers resume search for 129 missing after ferry capsized</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2dadb96f5fef0ecf17515d9ab038cf1eb4d7a5f5d7cbef61d32a64a5bbf0b00</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T08:57:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-indonesia-rescuers-resume-search-for-129-missing-after-ferry-capsized--3f97e7973f03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-indonesia-rescuers-resume-search-for-129-missing-after-ferry-capsized" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of Indonesian rescuers including the coast guard and the navy raced on Monday to board a passenger ship that capsized in the Java Sea over the weekend as they searched for 129 people still missing, officials said, with the confirmed death toll at six.</summary></entry></feed>
